WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:22.500
The refrigeration cycle is the foundation of everything you'll do in this trade.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:45.000
The metering device controls refrigerant flow into the evaporator. TXV adjusts
flow based on superheat using a sensing bulb on the suction line. Piston is a
fixed orifice providing constant restriction. TXV systems are charged by

00:00:45.000 --> 00:01:07.500
Here are the key terms. Write these down.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:30.000
TXV Sensing Bulb: Temperature sensor clamped to suction line controlling TXV
opening.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:52.500
Fixed Orifice: Piston with precisely sized hole providing constant restriction.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:02:15.000
Here's why this matters on the job: Knowing which metering device determines
your charging method. Wrong method gives wrong results.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:37.500
Watch out for these: Check data plate for TXV or piston. And — Restricted TXV
mimics low charge symptoms

00:02:37.500 --> 00:03:00.000
Before you move on — what happens to refrigerant in the evaporator? Don't look
it up. Think about it.

